- Please always use the F# best practices and make sure you dont add anything necessary.
- Make sure the code is always optimized and not doing unnecessary stuff.
- Make sure to look at the project file to see the f sharp version and use the latest features.
- Do not make mistakes or linting errors, make sure code is readable and has no linting errors. 
- Never use comments.
- Never remove functionality or logic unless specifically asked to.
- Always remove redundant code and redundant qualifiers when not needed.
- Never keep unnecesary paranthesis.
- Dont make mistakes with indentation.
- Plase use functions in the helpers fle where ever possible.
- Never use boxing
- Always use async when possible, never run anything in sync unless it is the only way to do it.
- Always use the best F# formatting for readability
- Always use the new _. syntax for lambda functions where possible